\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The SemCP pipeline. Given a prompt $x$, an LLM generates $K$ candidate responses. These are partitioned into semantic equivalence classes via bidirectional entailment, scored using learned RBF kernels in embedding space, and calibrated to produce prediction sets with formal coverage guarantees over meanings rather than strings.}}{8}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:framework}{{1}{8}{The SemCP pipeline. Given a prompt $x$, an LLM generates $K$ candidate responses. These are partitioned into semantic equivalence classes via bidirectional entailment, scored using learned RBF kernels in embedding space, and calibrated to produce prediction sets with formal coverage guarantees over meanings rather than strings}{figure.1}{}}
